    rdf:value """Wednesday, Oct. 28, 1908
Dorchester. 
We came in to engage rooms and Isabella joined us and we talked for two  hours . Then we were ill-advised enough to go out to hear Dr. Bigelow lecture on Buddhism, but the dullest, most primeval sort of lecture. It nearly killed  us ! We had a glimpse of the Fogg Museum beforehand and met Joseph Breck. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 324 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1908> .

